    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Convert Data Types\r\n\r\nThe program loads `survey_data.csv` into a DataFrame named `survey_data`.\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program. Examine the `Height` and `Join Date` columns and the provided graph.\r\n\r\n2. Use AI Tutor to convert `Height` to `int64` and display the updated dataset information.\r\n\r\n3. Examine AI Tutor’s changes, then run the program.\r\n\r\n   * What happened to the decimal values?\r\n\r\n4. Use AI Tutor to convert `Height` back to `float64`. Run the program again.\r\n\r\n   * Were the original decimal values restored?\r\n\r\n5. Use AI Tutor to convert `Join Date` with `pd.to_datetime()` and verify the final data types.\r\n\r\n6. Examine the two conversion expressions and run the program.\r\n\r\n   * How is the syntax for `astype()` different from `pd.to_datetime()`?\r\n   * How did converting `Join Date` affect the graph?",
